{"results": [{"source_id": "kb:collaboration#shared-mailbox-or-calendar-access-requests", "score": 0.238, "excerpt": "Shared mailbox or calendar access requests
A request to be added to a team or shared mailbox is routine self-service once a manager or an
existing delegate approves it. A request for someone's individual mailbox is not the same category;
see the access-and-identity runbook."}, {"source_id": "kb:emr#emr-sign-in-fails-but-the-network-account-works", "score": 0.137, "excerpt": "EMR sign-in fails but the network account works
This is usually an EMR-specific credential, not the network password. Do not reset the network
password for this. Escalate to Clinical Applications Support with the exact error text."}, {"source_id": "kb:security#possible-credential-compromise-password-entered-on-a-fake-site-unfamiliar-sign-ins", "score": 0.113, "excerpt": "Possible credential compromise (password entered on a fake site, unfamiliar sign-ins)
Treat as urgent regardless of how minor the user thinks it is. A password reset alone is not
sufficient if MFA may also be compromised (e.g. the user also approved an unexpected MFA prompt);
that combination needs a security review, not just a reset."}]}
